A __CVV-final-rafsi__ consists of a ((Morphology: consonants|consonant)),  a ((Morphology: vowels|stressed-vowel)), an ((Morphology: vowels|apostrophe)) and a ((Morphology: vowels|final-syllable)) ((Morphology: vowels|vowel)) (CVhV).

A __short-final-rafsi__  is a ((Morphology: vowels|final-syllable)) consisting of a  ((Morphology: consonants|consonant)) and a ((Morphology: vowels|diphthong)) (CVV), or an  ((Morphology: consonants|initial-pair)) and a ((Morphology: vowels|vowel)) (CCV).

An __initial-rafsi__ is an ((Morphology: extended rafsi|extended-rafsi)), a __y-rafsi__, or a __y-less-rafsi__ not the beginning of ((Morphology: extended rafsi|any-extended-rafsi)).

A __stressed-initial-rafsi__ is a ((Morphology: extended rafsi|stressed-extended-rafsi)), a __stressed-y-rafsi__, or a __stressed-y-less-rafsi__. 

A __y-rafsi__ is a CCVCy, CVCCy or CVCy form with an ((Morphology: vowels|unstressed-vowel)), possibly followed by an ((Morphology: vowels|apostrophe)) (in case a vowel-initial ((Morphology: extended rafsi|extended-rafsi)) follows).

A __stressed-y-rafsi__ is a CCVCy, CVCCy or CVCy form with a ((Morphology: vowels|stressed-vowel)). In this case an ((Morphology: vowels|apostrophe)) can't follow because there are no single-syllable ((Morphology: extended rafsi|extended-rafsi)) that could come after it.

A __y-less-rafsi__ is a CVC, CCV or CVV form rafsi with ((Morphology: vowels|unstressed-vowel))s such that they are not the beginning of a __y-rafsi__ and such that they are not followed by ((Morphology: extended rafsi|any-extended-rafsi)).

A __stressed-y-less-rafsi__ is a CVC, CCV or CVV form rafsi with final ((Morphology: vowels|stressed-vowel))s such that they are not the beginning of a __stressed-y-rafsi__.

stressed-CVV-rafsi <- consonant (unstressed-vowel h stressed-vowel / stressed-diphthong) r-hyphen?

A stressed or unstressed CVV form rafsi include a possible __r-hyphen__ at the end. 

An __r-hyphen__ is an 'r' if what follows is a consonant and an 'n' if what follows is an 'r'.
